{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:retain-candidate-refs:1", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "retain-candidate-refs", "index": 1, "text": "Every call to Repository.commit_candidate from execution.run_serial and from the worker-completion branch of parallel.run_parallel leaves the new candidate commit named by a ref; these are the only two production call sites.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:retain-candidate-refs:2", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "retain-candidate-refs", "index": 2, "text": "Every call to Repository.prepare_integration from execution.run_serial, from the integration-dispatch branch of parallel.run_parallel, and from its recovery candidate-reuse branch leaves the integration revision named by a ref; these are the only three production call sites.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:retain-candidate-refs:3", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "retain-candidate-refs", "index": 3, "text": "Refs are written under one refs/anvil/ namespace keyed by run ID and attempt ID, are created by the supervisor on the coordinator thread only, and are never created inside a worker worktree or by a worker turn.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": true, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:retain-candidate-refs:4", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "retain-candidate-refs", "index": 4, "text": "A run whose ledger predates this change still resumes, and no acceptance, rejection, retry, or recovery decision reads or requires one of these refs.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": true, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed-revised"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:retain-candidate-refs:5", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "retain-candidate-refs", "index": 5, "text": "Tests assert that after an accepted ticket, after a review rejection, and after a verification failure, the recorded candidate_sha and integration_sha are each reachable from a ref, so git prune --expire=now cannot drop them.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": true, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:reap-candidate-refs:1", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "reap-candidate-refs", "index": 1, "text": "A read-only subcommand lists every retained ref with its run ID, attempt ID, ticket ID, revision, and whether that attempt was accepted, and exits without changing any ref.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:reap-candidate-refs:2", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "reap-candidate-refs", "index": 2, "text": "The same subcommand deletes the retained refs of one named run when explicitly asked, and reports how many it removed.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:reap-candidate-refs:3", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "reap-candidate-refs", "index": 3, "text": "Deleting retained refs never moves the managed branch, never writes the ledger, and never removes a revision that the managed branch or any run directory's recorded acceptance still names.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": true, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:reap-candidate-refs:4", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "reap-candidate-refs", "index": 4, "text": "Deletion is explicit: no run, resume, or status invocation removes a retained ref as a side effect.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "candidate-retention.json:reap-candidate-refs:5", "file": "candidate-retention.json", "task": "reap-candidate-refs", "index": 5, "text": "Tests cover listing a mix of accepted and rejected attempts, deleting one run's refs while another run's refs survive, and refusing to delete a revision reachable from the managed branch.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": true, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:environment-exclusion-set:1", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "environment-exclusion-set", "index": 1, "text": "The managed environment builder accepts an explicit exclusion set and omits exactly those variables while preserving all other non-Git variables and PATH.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:environment-exclusion-set:2", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "environment-exclusion-set", "index": 2, "text": "An absent or empty exclusion set produces exactly the environment callers receive today.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:environment-exclusion-set:3", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "environment-exclusion-set", "index": 3, "text": "Unit tests cover excluding present variables, naming absent variables, and case-sensitive matching.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": true, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:apply-credential-exclusion:1", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "apply-credential-exclusion", "index": 1, "text": "A run configuration field names the variables to withhold; absent or empty changes nothing for existing runs.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:apply-credential-exclusion:2", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "apply-credential-exclusion", "index": 2, "text": "Every managed subprocess launch builds its environment with that exclusion set: agent implementation turns, independent review turns, verification check commands, the adaptive session's per-attempt runners, the adaptive profile preflight probe in adaptive_runtime, and the same preflight probe reached through `anvil doctor --config`.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:apply-credential-exclusion:3", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "apply-credential-exclusion", "index": 3, "text": "Leakage tests prove excluded variables are absent from subprocess environments, from subprocess argv, and from recorded command artifacts.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": true, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:apply-credential-exclusion:4", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "apply-credential-exclusion", "index": 4, "text": "README.md documents the new field beside the existing run configuration fields, and docs/AGENT_ADAPTERS.md no longer states that doctor has no exclusion set to apply, which holds only without --config.", "procedure": "artifact", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:apply-credential-exclusion:5", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "apply-credential-exclusion", "index": 5, "text": "Existing serial, parallel, adaptive and recovery tests remain green with no exclusion configured.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:ledger-query-layer:1", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "ledger-query-layer", "index": 1, "text": "Queries exist for run summaries, per-run task summaries, ticket attempts, and events after a given event ID.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:ledger-query-layer:2", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "ledger-query-layer", "index": 2, "text": "Pages default to 100 rows and reject requests above 500 rows.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:ledger-query-layer:3", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "ledger-query-layer", "index": 3, "text": "Reads succeed and stay consistent while a supervisor is actively committing events to the same ledger.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:ledger-query-layer:4", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "ledger-query-layer", "index": 4, "text": "Runs created by earlier Anvil versions are readable through the same queries.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integration-config-and-freeze:1", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integration-config-and-freeze", "index": 1, "text": "A versioned integration configuration and a run-level integrations object validate against packaged JSON Schemas and matching runtime checks; runs without the object behave exactly as before.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integration-config-and-freeze:2", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integration-config-and-freeze", "index": 2, "text": "Environment, credential-helper, and OS credential store references resolve to typed records with authentication scheme and required identity metadata; a Bitbucket API token without its Atlassian email is rejected without trying another scheme.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integration-config-and-freeze:3", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integration-config-and-freeze", "index": 3, "text": "Run creation freezes connection identities, workflow policy, credential reference names, and publication policy into run artifacts and binds the snapshot digest to a committed ledger event.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integration-config-and-freeze:4", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integration-config-and-freeze", "index": 4, "text": "Configured credential variables are passed to the subprocess exclusion set and never appear in run config, ledger payloads, or reports.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integration-config-and-freeze:5", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integration-config-and-freeze", "index": 5, "text": "Editing the repository configuration after run creation does not change the frozen snapshot that resume reads.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": false, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integrations-doctor-github:1", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integrations-doctor-github", "index": 1, "text": "A code-host contract exposes repository resolution and capability/permission discovery, and the GitHub adapter implements the read paths against a fake HTTP provider with documented API version.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integrations-doctor-github:2", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integrations-doctor-github", "index": 2, "text": "The doctor command resolves the configured repository to its canonical identity, reports missing grants and unsupported capabilities explicitly, and performs no remote writes or model calls.", "procedure": "execution", "unbounded_absence": true, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed-revised"}
{"uid": "delivery-dashboard.json:integrations-doctor-github:3", "file": "delivery-dashboard.json", "task": "integrations-doctor-github", "index": 3, "text": "HTTP requests carry a pinned API version, respect a 15-second timeout, and refuse to forward authorization to a redirect outside the expected host.", "procedure": "reading", "unbounded_absence": false, "joins_claims": true, "self_gradable": false, "labeled_by": "model-proposed"}
